From f956374c03f7232e01e7480423a2a5174c42f1dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:04:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Code screens: say why one cannot run and show its JSON screen
 instead; log the screens.wasm a mod brings

A menu whose screen is drawn by code and whose code could not run (no screens.wasm registered, the component not
loading, open refused, the open menu's panel not found) drew nothing: no panel, no slot frames, no log line, and
horizon-ctl state's screen_code was null. Now:
- the reason is warned once per menu and kept: horizon-ctl state's screen_code has the menu and error even when the
  screen never opened;
- the menu's JSON screen (its widgets and the slots' frames) is drawn and pressed instead, with a red line under the
  panel saying why;
- loading content says which menus a mod draws by code and the size of its screens.wasm, warns when a mod has menus
  drawn by code but no screens.wasm, or a screens.wasm without capability screen.
- HORIZON_ASYNC_STARTUP=1 keeps the loading screen's startup (the one Android always takes) under the control socket,
  to test that path on the desktop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
